MICHAELSON:	When you attacked the base on Titan, did anything catch your attention?  

ROBERTS:	Shaw’s tactics. Grigg, our most junior officer, was being sent in to retrieve sensitive data - and despite being the most senior, I was running interference. My mission to cut off their communications started at the same time as Grigg’s infiltration, so I wouldn't have been able to prevent them calling for help until the very last minute. 

MICHAELSON:	 Were you ever made aware of the base’s purpose?

ROBERTS:	All I knew was that it contained the location of the armoury. Grigg came back running his mouth about all sorts of research, but nobody seemed to be able to make sense of him. All of the data he retrieved got turned over to Baker for analysis. 

MICHAELSON:	Corporal Baker denies having received anything, and what records we've recovered confirm that - and yet, the nature of the mission you were deployed on suggests advance knowledge of the base’s purpose.

ROBERTS:	I get the feeling you know more than you're telling me.

MICHAELSON:	That is usually how these sort of interviews work, Lieutenant.